s events#Procedure#{11}":[601,602],"#Server-side script use cases#Using custom queues to process events#Procedure#{12}":[603,604],"#Server-side script use cases#Using custom queues to process events#Procedure#{13}":[605,606],"#Server-side script use cases#Using custom queues to process events#Procedure#{14}":[607,612],"#Server-side script use cases#Using custom queues to process events#Procedure#{15}":[613,614],"#Server-side script use cases#Using custom queues to process events#Procedure#{16}":[615,624],"#Server-side script use cases#Related":[625,631],"#Server-side script use cases#Related#{1}":[627,627],"#Server-side script use cases#Related#{2}":[628,628],"#Server-side script use cases#Related#{3}":[629,629],"#Server-side script use cases#Related#{4}":[630,631]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Useful scripts","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/scripts/usefulScripts.md","line":26},{"title":"update","target":"r_Update","line":67},{"title":"forum","target":"http://community.service-now.com/","line":79},{"title":"Creating and using schedules","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_UseSchedules.md","line":122},{"title":"Define a relative duration","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/t_DefineARelativeDuration.md","line":204},{"title":"script includes","target":"c_ScriptIncludes","line":392},{"title":"GlideUser","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/GUserAPI.md","line":474},{"title":"API reference","target":"api-reference","line":509},{"title":"GSLog\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/GSLogBoth.md","line":509},{"title":"Debugging scripts","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/scripts/script-debug-overview.md","line":511},{"title":"GlideDateTime","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/scripts/p_GlideServerAPIs.md","line":558},{"title":"GlideDate - Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/GlideDateAPI.md","line":559},{"title":"GlideDate - Scoped","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideDateScopedAPI.md","line":560},{"title":"GlideDateTime - Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideDateTimeAPI.md","line":561},{"title":"GlideDateTime - Scoped","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideDateTimeScoped.md","line":562},{"title":"GlideElement - Global","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideElementAPI.md","line":563},{"title":"GlideElement - Scoped","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideElementScopedAPI.md","line":564},{"title":"GlideTime - Scoped","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/server-api-reference/c_GlideTimeScopedAPI.md","line":565},{"title":"Insert","target":"r_Insert","line":599},{"title":"Script includes","target":"c_ScriptIncludes","line":627},{"title":"API reference","target":"api-reference","line":628},{"title":"insert","target":"r_Insert","line":629},{"title":"update","target":"r_Update","line":630}],"metadata":{"title":"Server-side script use cases","description":"Use cases for server-side scripts include logging output, getting user objects, and modifying date/time values.A catalog item has been requested, and the attached workflow contains a run script activity that populates a value in the scratchpad. From a business rule running on the requested item, you want to retrieve or set scratchpad values.Assign a service catalog item to the database group if it uses a delivery plan that has a catalog task that is assigned to the desktop group.Often you may need to provide users with a way to specify when a task or process is due. Using the DurationCalculator script include, you can calculate the due date using either a simple duration or relative duration.How much work is required to complete a task can be expressed as a \"relative duration\".This business rule and script example demonstrate how to calculate a simple duration.An example of a relative duration calculation script.You can implement a relative duration by creating the cmn\\_relative\\_duration table and the DurationCalculator script include.The cmn\\_relative\\_duration table supports the definition of a due date as either a duration of time or a relative duration.In a business rule or other server script, the gs.getUser\\(\\) method returns a user object. The user object is an internal representation of the currently logged in user and provides information about the user and various utility functions.GSLog is a script include that simplifies script logging and debugging by implementing levels of log output, selectable by per-caller identified sys\\_properties values.This example demonstrates how to modify a GlideDateTime field value using a server-side script.You can use custom queues for applications that create a large volume of events or events that take a long time to process. This task shows how to create a custom queue, its monitoring process, and use a script to send events to the queue.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/scripts/useful-server-side-